<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Active Reasoning</span> requires LLMs to interact with external
sources and actively acquire missing information to solve complex tasks.
Prior work has improved LLMs’ ability to handle ambiguity and incompleteness through making clarification and information-seeking actions. For example, Proactive CoT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al., 2023</a>)</cite> prompts LLMs to identify ambiguous problems
and generate clarification questions, while UoT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> quantifies the contribution of each question in reducing uncertainty.
However, challenges remain when transitioning from LLMs’ single-turn success to multi-turn active reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwan et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Badola et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, even with several advanced strategies such as tree-based searching
or post-training approaches, as highlighted in existing works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. There have been existing works which target RL on active reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al., 2026</a>)</cite>. In our work, we identify a unique mechanism named information self-locking, which is sourced from a structural
failure of credit assignment with bidirectional coupling between action selection (AS) and belief tracking (BT). This is consistent with empirical observations from real-world agentic use. For example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025b)</a></cite> uncovers the phenomenon specific to search agents: systematic deficiencies in search behaviors arise under outcome-only training and ultimately degrade final answer quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Credit Assignment and Multi-turn RL.</span>
Credit assignment is crucial to long-horizon or multi-turn RL.
Existing methods have extensively explored
rule-based approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dou et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite> to shape intermediate rewards.
Several recent works also proposed to measure the progress of stepwise actions toward overall task completion as intermediate rewards.
Specifically, CURIO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wan et al., 2025</a>)</cite> constructs a potential function over an ideal belief state to assign intermediate rewards, assuming that the latent state space is finite and enumerable.
Sotopia-RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> relies on reward labeling with proprietary LLMs. SPA-RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> trains reward models for intermediate rewards by enforcing a summation constraint with respect to the final outcome reward.
In our work, instead of working on complicated reward shaping or resorting to external models, we leverage easy-to-use binary directional critiques to make a minimal injection to policy gradient which is mathematically derived from a margin-aware auxiliary objective, in order to provide non-degenerate and stable learning signals to help agents escape from self-locking.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>More Details on the Theory</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Notations &amp; Problem Setup</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">active reasoning</em>, where an LLM agent interacts with an external environment to acquire missing
information and infer the underlying solution through multi-turn interaction. This can be modeled as a POMDP
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{Q},\mathcal{O},T,O,R,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{Q},\mathcal{O},T,O,R,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the space of unobservable latent states, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> the action space, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> the observation space, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(s^{\prime}\mid s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> the transition dynamics, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(o\mid s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(o\mid s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> the observation model, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> the reward function, and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> the discount factor.
In our setting, the latent state is fixed within each episode of horizon <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We assume deterministic feedback: for all <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,q)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,q)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the observation kernel <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(\cdot\mid s,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\cdot\mid s,q)</annotation></semantics></math> is a point mass at <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=\mathsf{O}(s,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=\mathsf{O}(s,q)</annotation></semantics></math>; in particular,
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Belief.</span>
We work with a belief-state abstraction where the agent is associated with an explicit <em id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">model belief</em>
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math> which represents the agent’s internal understanding of the latent state and what information remains missing at each turn <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\ldots,H\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\ldots,H\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that this abstraction does <em id="A2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> assume the agent internally stores
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>; rather, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a well-defined object induced
by the model parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> and the interaction history, which we use
purely for theoretical analysis.
We quantify truth-aligned confidence by the potential <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(b):=b(s^{\star})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(b):=b(s^{\star})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which measures the model’s confidence mass assigned to the true latent
state and serves as our working notion of belief quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Trajectory.</span>
Agentic behaviour in active reasoning can be decomposed into two coupled processes:
<span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action Selection (AS)</span> and <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Belief Tracking (BT)</span>.
A single agent with parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> induces:
(i) a BT-channel <em id="A2.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">belief update</em> kernel <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{U}</annotation></semantics></math> that produces the next belief given the latest interaction, and
(ii) an AS-channel <em id="A2.SS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">query policy</em> <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> that selects queries conditioned on the current belief.
Concretely, define the BT-conditioning context <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as a fixed initial context
(e.g., task instructions), and
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t+1}:=(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t},o_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t+1}:=(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t},o_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>
for
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each turn <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulted <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">belief-MDP</span> evolves via query generation
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
observation
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>,
and belief update
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We write the full trajectory <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{0},o_{0},\;b_{1}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{1},o_{1},\;\ldots,\;b_{H-1}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{H-1},o_{H-1},\;b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{0},o_{0},\;b_{1}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{1},o_{1},\;\ldots,\;b_{H-1}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{H-1},o_{H-1},\;b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where the trajectory likelihood factorizes as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\omega}(\tau)=\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{0})\;\prod_{t=0}^{H-1}\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\;\prod_{t=0}^{H-1}\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t+1}),\,\,\,\text{where}\,\,\,c_{t+1}=(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t},o_{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.677em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.510em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\omega}(\tau)=\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{0})\;\prod_{t=0}^{H-1}\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\;\prod_{t=0}^{H-1}\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t+1}),\,\,\,\text{where}\,\,\,c_{t+1}=(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t},o_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Outcome reward.</span>
The environment returns an outcome reward <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\tau)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\tau)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., correctness of the inferred solution).
We assume the expected reward is a (non-decreasing) function of the terminal potential:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a non-decreasing <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:[0,1]\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:[0,1]\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> s.t.,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[R(\tau)\ \middle|\ b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}\right]=f\!\left(\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.427em;" width="0.427em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[R(\tau)\ \middle|\ b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}\right]=f\!\left(\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Two Capability Indices</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Oracle Bayesian belief.</span>
To decouple AS informativeness from the model’s BT mechanism,
we introduce an oracle (Bayesian), theoretically optimal belief update process.
Given deterministic feedback <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q)</annotation></semantics></math>, define the Bayesian update operator
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{BayesUpd}(\cdot,q,o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡𝖺𝗒𝖾𝗌𝖴𝗉𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{BayesUpd}(\cdot,q,o)</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\mathsf{BayesUpd}(b,q,o)\big)(s)\;:=\;\frac{b(s)\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathsf{O}(s,q)=o\}}{\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}b(s^{\prime})\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathsf{O}(s^{\prime},q)=o\}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡𝖺𝗒𝖾𝗌𝖴𝗉𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝖮</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝖮</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\mathsf{BayesUpd}(b,q,o)\big)(s)\;:=\;\frac{b(s)\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathsf{O}(s,q)=o\}}{\sum_{s^{\prime}\in\mathcal{S}}b(s^{\prime})\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathsf{O}(s^{\prime},q)=o\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Oracle-belief MDP.</span>
For analysis purposes only, we consider an oracle-belief MDP that evolves under
Bayesian belief updates while sharing the same query policy as the agent.
Fix a prior <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}}(s^{\star})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}}(s^{\star})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each turn <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
an oracle-belief trajectory evolves as
query generation conditioned on oracle belief
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
observation
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>,
and
Bayesian belief update
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{B}}=\mathsf{BayesUpd}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t},o_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖡𝖺𝗒𝖾𝗌𝖴𝗉𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{B}}=\mathsf{BayesUpd}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t},o_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This yields
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\mathrm{B}}:=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{0},o_{0},\;b_{1}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{1},o_{1},\;\ldots,\;b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\mathrm{B}}:=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{0},o_{0},\;b_{1}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{1},o_{1},\;\ldots,\;b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Notably, the oracle-belief MDP is introduced solely for analysis, aiming to isolate AS information supply, and we do not require the actual agent to access oracle belief <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now quantify the informativeness of a query policy by the belief improvement
it induces under the oracle-belief dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a oracle-belief MDP trajectory
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\mathrm{B}}=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{0},o_{0},\ldots,b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\mathrm{B}}=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{0},o_{0},\ldots,b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math>
induced by the query policy
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
Bayesian belief dynamics <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{BayesUpd}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡𝖺𝗒𝖾𝗌𝖴𝗉𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{BayesUpd}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define one-step oracle belief progress as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}:=\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}:=\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the theoretical AS informativeness of a query policy <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>
as the expected total improvement in oracle belief quality under the oracle-belief MDP,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{\mathrm{B}}}\big[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}I^{\mathrm{B}}_{t}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{\mathrm{B}}}\big[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}I^{\mathrm{B}}_{t}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We next characterize how much of the theoretical supplied information is actually absorbed
by the agent model’s belief-tracking dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For an on-policy trajectory <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{0},o_{0},\ldots,b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{0},o_{0},\ldots,b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> generated under <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>,
define the one-step potential change at turn <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}:=\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}:=\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We decompose <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> into its one-sided components:
the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">absorbed</span> belief progress
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}:=(\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}:=(\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">self-destructive</span> belief drift
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}:=(-\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}:=(-\Delta\Psi_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Only the redeemable component contributes positively to belief improvement.
The training-level belief-tracking (BT) index is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\big[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\big[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To relate AS informativeness to BT progress under learning dynamics,
we impose the following mild regularity assumptions.
Each assumption is accompanied by a brief intuition clarifying its role:
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Asmp. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Assumption B.4. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a></span> states that harmful belief drift is independent of the specific
query chosen, and is instead driven by deficiencies in the agent’s BT
mechanism.
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Asmp. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption B.5. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a></span> upper-bounds the amount of belief progress that can be absorbed
in a single step, and further ties such progress to the evidence revealed under the oracle belief dynamics.
<span id="A2.SS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Asmp. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Assumption B.6. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a></span> enforces a Lipschitz-type stability of future belief quality
with respect to the current potential, reflecting a conservative propagation
of belief improvements under weak belief-tracking.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any turn <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and any query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional expectation of the self-destructive drift given the current belief
is invariant to the query choice, i.e.,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t}=q\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t}=q\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>
almost surely for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any turn <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\max}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\max}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that
along on-policy rollouts, the conditional expectation satisfies
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t}\right]\leq C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t}\right]\leq C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>
almost surely over the realized query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;
and there exists a constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{U}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{U}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that along on-policy rollouts,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t}\right]\ \leq\ \kappa_{U}\cdot I_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t}\right]\ \leq\ \kappa_{U}\cdot I_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>
a.s. over the realized query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t&lt;t^{\prime}\leq H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t&lt;t^{\prime}\leq H</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist a constant
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for and any realizable model beliefs
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,\tilde{b}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,\tilde{b}\in\Delta(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math> at turn <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big|\ \mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathrm{M}})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathrm{M}})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=\tilde{b}\right]\ \Big|\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,\big|\Psi(b)-\Psi(\tilde{b})\big|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big|\ \mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathrm{M}})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t^{\prime}}^{\mathrm{M}})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=\tilde{b}\right]\ \Big|\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,\big|\Psi(b)-\Psi(\tilde{b})\big|.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Locking regime.</span>
We formalize the notion of self-locking via a two-dimensional low-information <span id="A2.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">plus</span> low-BT region:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Locking regime)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For given thresholds <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the locking regime as the subset of parameter space
characterized by simultaneously low theoretical action-selection informativeness and low belief-tracking capability:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}\;:=\;\big\{\omega\in\Omega:\ \mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\leq\delta,\ \ C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\leq\varepsilon\big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}\;:=\;\big\{\omega\in\Omega:\ \mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\leq\delta,\ \ C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\leq\varepsilon\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This region represents a two-dimensional low-information plus low-BT regime in which
neither the query policy nor the belief-tracking dynamics can induce substantial positive progress.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze local training dynamics within the locking regime,
we require a mild first-order regularity of the two indices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.8</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local first-order expandability of indices)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and consider <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exist constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{I},G_{C}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{I},G_{C}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\omega^{\prime}-\omega\|=O(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\omega^{\prime}-\omega\|=O(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
the following first-order expansions hold uniformly over <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega^{\prime})=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \omega^{\prime}-\omega\rangle+o(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega^{\prime})=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \omega^{\prime}-\omega\rangle+o(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega^{\prime})=C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)+\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ \omega^{\prime}-\omega\rangle+o(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega^{\prime})=C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)+\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ \omega^{\prime}-\omega\rangle+o(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(\eta)/\eta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(\eta)/\eta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Projected Drifts and the 2D Locking Regime</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Policy-gradient decomposition of the outcome objective.</span>
We begin by expressing the outcome-based policy gradient in a form that
admits a decomposition across the AS and BT channels.
With the outcome objective <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}[R(\tau)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}[R(\tau)]</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\omega}J(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\Big[R(\tau)\,\nabla_{\omega}\log p_{\omega}(\tau)\Big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\omega}J(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\Big[R(\tau)\,\nabla_{\omega}\log p_{\omega}(\tau)\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and hence (via Eq. <a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ B.1 Notations &amp; Problem Setup ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\omega}\log p_{\omega}(\tau)=\sum_{t=0}^{H}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})+\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\omega}\log p_{\omega}(\tau)=\sum_{t=0}^{H}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})+\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We next impose a mild regularity assumption to control the policy-gradient magnitude.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.9</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist finite constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{Q}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{Q}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{U}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{U}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\|\leq G_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\|\leq G_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\|\leq G_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\|\leq G_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>
almost surely under <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Channel-isolated Stage-wise advantages.</span> As mentioned before, we have decomposed the agentic behavior into two coupled but conceptually
distinct channels: AS and BT.
 To characterize how outcome-based training signals propagate through each channel, we introduce
channel-isolated stage-wise value functions, in which the other channel is treated as <span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">part of the induced environment dynamics</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For the BT channel, the belief state <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself is regarded as the decision variable.
For <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\ldots,H\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\ldots,H\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q^{J,U}_{t}(c,b):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[R(\tau)\mid c_{t}=c,\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right],\qquad V^{J,U}_{t}(c):=\mathbb{E}_{b\sim\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c)}\!\left[Q^{J,U}_{t}(c,b)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>U</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{J,U}_{t}(c,b):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[R(\tau)\mid c_{t}=c,\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right],\qquad V^{J,U}_{t}(c):=\mathbb{E}_{b\sim\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c)}\!\left[Q^{J,U}_{t}(c,b)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">and the corresponding advantage</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{J,U}_{t}(c,b):=Q^{J,U}_{t}(c,b)-V^{J,U}_{t}(c)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{J,U}_{t}(c,b):=Q^{J,U}_{t}(c,b)-V^{J,U}_{t}(c).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, for the AS channel, the query <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as the decision variable.
For <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[R(\tau)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right],\qquad V^{J,Q}_{t}(b):=\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b)}\!\left[Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[R(\tau)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right],\qquad V^{J,Q}_{t}(b):=\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b)}\!\left[Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with advantage</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q):=Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-V^{J,Q}_{t}(b)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q):=Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-V^{J,Q}_{t}(b).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Channel-isolated outcome update directions.</span>
Using the above definitions, the policy-gradient update directions induced by the outcome objective <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>
can be written as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{J,Q}(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\,A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\right]\quad g_{J,U}(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\,A^{J,U}_{t}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{J,Q}(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\,A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\right]\quad g_{J,U}(\omega):=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\,A^{J,U}_{t}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Accordingly, define the query-channel projected update
<math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\ :=\ \omega+\eta\,g_{J,Q}(\omega)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\ :=\ \omega+\eta\,g_{J,Q}(\omega),</annotation></semantics></math>
and the BT-channel projected update
<math id="A2.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega)\ :=\ \omega+\eta\,g_{J,U}(\omega)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega)\ :=\ \omega+\eta\,g_{J,U}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math>
Note that these are <em id="A2.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">virtual</em> updates used for only mechanism analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by bounding the channel-isolated outcome advantages,
which quantify the strength of the outcome-based learning signal
available to each channel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.10</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(AS-channel outcome advantages)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume Assumptions <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ B.1 Notations &amp; Problem Setup ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Assumption B.4. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption B.5. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, and
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Assumption B.6. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> hold,
then for any on-policy executed query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> at turn <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\big|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\big|\right]\ \leq\ L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\big|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\big|\right]\ \leq\ L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math>
Moreover, under Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Assumption B.9. ‣ B.3 Projected Drifts and the 2D Locking Regime ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\ \leq\ K_{Q}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\ \leq\ K_{Q}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{Q}:=H\,G_{Q}\,L_{R}\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{Q}:=H\,G_{Q}\,L_{R}\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.11</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(BT-channel outcome advantages)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume Assumptions <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ B.1 Notations &amp; Problem Setup ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Assumption B.4. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption B.5. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, and
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Assumption B.6. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> hold,
then for any on-policy generated belief <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> at turn <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\big|A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big|\right]\ \leq\ 2L_{R}\Big(C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ +\ \kappa_{U}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\big|A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big|\right]\ \leq\ 2L_{R}\Big(C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ +\ \kappa_{U}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math>
Moreover, under Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Assumption B.9. ‣ B.3 Projected Drifts and the 2D Locking Regime ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a>,
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\ \leq\ K_{U,I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ +\ K_{U,C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\ \leq\ K_{U,I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ +\ K_{U,C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{U,I}:=2(H+1)\,G_{U}\,L_{R}\kappa_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{U,I}:=2(H+1)\,G_{U}\,L_{R}\kappa_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{U,C}:=2(H+1)\,G_{U}\,L_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{U,C}:=2(H+1)\,G_{U}\,L_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now translate the channel-wise gradient bounds into one-step projected drifts
of the two capability indices within the locking regime.
For convenience, we denote by <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{Q}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{Q}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{U}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{U}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> the positive parts of
the one-step changes induced by the projected updates <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.12</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(AS projected drift is controlled by BT level)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption B.8 (Local first-order expandability of indices). ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a> and the conclusion of Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Proposition B.10 (AS-channel outcome advantages). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a>,
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ :=\ \big(\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega))-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\big)_{+}\ \leq\ \eta\,\alpha\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ +\ o(\eta),\qquad\alpha:=G_{I}K_{Q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ :=\ \big(\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega))-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\big)_{+}\ \leq\ \eta\,\alpha\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ +\ o(\eta),\qquad\alpha:=G_{I}K_{Q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.13</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(BT projected drift is controlled by AS and BT levels)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption B.8 (Local first-order expandability of indices). ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a> and the conclusion of Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem11" title="Proposition B.11 (BT-channel outcome advantages). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>,
for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ :=\ \big(C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega))-C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\big)_{+}\ \leq\ \eta\Big(\beta_{I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ +\ \beta_{C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\Big)\ +\ o(\eta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ :=\ \big(C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega))-C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\big)_{+}\ \leq\ \eta\Big(\beta_{I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ +\ \beta_{C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\Big)\ +\ o(\eta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{I}:=G_{C}\,K_{U,I},\qquad\beta_{C}:=G_{C}\,K_{U,C}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{I}:=G_{C}\,K_{U,I},\qquad\beta_{C}:=G_{C}\,K_{U,C}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now combine the channel-wise projected drift bounds into a unified
two-dimensional description of the local training dynamics
within the locking regime.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.14</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(2D one-sided self-locking)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and consider <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the conclusions of Propositions <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem12" title="Proposition B.12 (AS projected drift is controlled by BT level). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.12</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition B.13 (BT projected drift is controlled by AS and BT levels). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>,
the one-sided projected drifts satisfy the following componentwise inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\\[2.0pt]
\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\end{pmatrix}\ \preceq\ \eta\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\alpha\\
\beta_{I}&amp;\beta_{C}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\\[2.0pt]
C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\end{pmatrix}\ +\ o(\eta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>α</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\\[2.0pt]
\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\end{pmatrix}\ \preceq\ \eta\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\alpha\\
\beta_{I}&amp;\beta_{C}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\\[2.0pt]
C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\end{pmatrix}\ +\ o(\eta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\preceq</annotation></semantics></math> denotes elementwise inequality.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.15</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem14" title="Theorem B.14 (2D one-sided self-locking). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a> controls <math id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{Q}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{Q}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{U}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{U}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,
the <em id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">positive parts</em> of the projected drifts.
Note that our theoretical result does not assert that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot decrease, oscillate,
or be affected by algorithmic stabilizers (entropy bonuses, clipping, weight decay, etc.).
Rather, it formalizes self-locking as the <span id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">absence of a strong upward training signal</span> inside the low-information and low-BT regime:
even when improvements happen, the theorem shows they can only be of small magnitude,
scaling linearly with the current levels <math id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark B.16</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The AS-side drift bound is purely BT-limited:
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ \lesssim\ \eta\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≲</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ \lesssim\ \eta\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus, when BT is weak, the query policy receives only a weak positive signal to increase informativeness
(consistent with the intuition that AS learning is masked by BT failures in Sec. <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 Failure modes in reinforcement learning training ‣ 2 Self-Locking in Active Reasoning ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>).
In contrast, the BT-side drift bound is <span id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">non-dual</span>:
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ \lesssim\ \eta\big(\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≲</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\ \lesssim\ \eta\big(\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\big),</annotation></semantics></math>
where the additional self-term <math id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> captures a “self-improvement” channel:
even under limited information supply, the BT mechanism can still realize some gains by better utilizing the same evidence.
At the same time, the presence of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> formalizes the bottleneck:
when AS information supply stays low, BT improvements cannot scale beyond the evidence-limited envelope,
yielding the empirically observed pattern that BT may improve early but tends to plateau once AS remains uninformative, as mentioned in Sec. <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 Failure modes in reinforcement learning training ‣ 2 Self-Locking in Active Reasoning ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.17</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{0}\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{0}\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m:=\max\{\alpha,\ \beta_{I}+\beta_{C}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m:=\max\{\alpha,\ \beta_{I}+\beta_{C}\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
defining</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\ :=\ \Bigg\lfloor\frac{1}{\eta m}\,\log\!\Bigg(\frac{\varepsilon+C\eta}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta}\Bigg)\Bigg\rfloor_{+}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\ :=\ \Bigg\lfloor\frac{1}{\eta m}\,\log\!\Bigg(\frac{\varepsilon+C\eta}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta}\Bigg)\Bigg\rfloor_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">any projected evolution consistent with the one-step drift bounds of
Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem14" title="Theorem B.14 (2D one-sided self-locking). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a>
cannot leave <math id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> within the first <math id="A2.Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> steps.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Why <span id="A2.SS5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AReW</span> breaks Information Self-locking</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this part, we characterize how and when <span id="A2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AReW</span> proposed in Sec. <a href="#S4" title="4 Breaking Self-Locking with Directions ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> breaks information self-locking effectively.
For simplicity,
we specialize to the AS (query-policy) side and consider only binary critiques
<math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}\in\{+1,-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}\in\{+1,-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> on query steps.
The analysis for the BT side is entirely analogous and omitted for brevity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Critique quality and oracle “good” queries.</span>
Recall that AS informativeness is measured by the theoretical index
<math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as the expected total improvement in oracle belief quality
under the oracle-belief MDP (Definition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition B.2. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>).
As discussed before, a query can be assessed independently of the LLM agent’s belief-tracking
mechanism <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{U}</annotation></semantics></math> by its effect on the terminal oracle confidence <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math> under the oracle-belief dynamics.
Specifically, we give the following definitions:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.18</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Oracle-good Query)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the setting of Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Notations &amp; Problem Setup ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, consider a oracle-belief MDP trajectory
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\mathrm{B}}=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{0},o_{0},\ldots,b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\mathrm{B}}=(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{0},o_{0},\ldots,b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math>
induced by the query policy
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
Bayesian belief dynamics <math id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{BayesUpd}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡𝖺𝗒𝖾𝗌𝖴𝗉𝖽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{BayesUpd}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the expected terminal oracle confidence following a query <math id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> at oracle belief <math id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{t}(b,q)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}(b,q)\;:=\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right].</annotation></semantics></math>
A query is oracle-good at step <math id="A2.Thmtheorem18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> if it yields a higher terminal oracle confidence than the policy
average at the same oracle belief, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\;&gt;\;\mathbb{E}_{q^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})}\!\left[m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q^{\prime})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\;&gt;\;\mathbb{E}_{q^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})}\!\left[m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q^{\prime})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By telescoping of oracle belief progress,
<math id="A2.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{B}}=\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{B}}=\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
the stepwise <em id="A2.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">AS advantage with respect to <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> is given by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})=m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})-\mathbb{E}_{q^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})}\!\left[m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q^{\prime})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})=m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})-\mathbb{E}_{q^{\prime}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})}\!\left[m_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q^{\prime})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which measures how much the chosen query improves the expected terminal oracle confidence
relative to the policy’s average choice at the same oracle belief.
We therefore define the <em id="A2.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">oracle direction label</em></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}:=\mathrm{sign}\!\big(A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\big)\in\{+1,-1\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.756em;" width="1.756em"><mi>sign</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}:=\mathrm{sign}\!\big(A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\big)\in\{+1,-1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p">indicating whether the step-<math id="A2.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> query contributes positively or negatively to
<math id="A2.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> under the oracle-belief dynamics.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Efficacy of <span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AReW</span> and weighted accuracy.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The critique label <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}\in\{+1,-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}\in\{+1,-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as an approximation of the oracle direction
label <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For critique injection to improve AS informativeness beyond outcome-only learning,
it is necessary that the injected signal aligns, on average, with the true stepwise
contributions to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, positive critique should be assigned more frequently to oracle-good
queries than to oracle-bad ones.
Moreover, different steps along the trajectory do not contribute equally to
AS informativeness.
This leads naturally to a notion of <span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">weighted accuracy</span> of the critique labels
with respect to the oracle direction labels.
The following proposition shows that, under a mild regularity condition,
the effectiveness of <span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AReW</span> in improving AS informativeness is fully determined
by this weighted accuracy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.19</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weighted accuracy characterizes <span id="A2.Thmtheorem19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AReW</span> improvement)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem19.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the setting of Sec. <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Injecting directional critiques into policy-gradient ‣ 4 Breaking Self-Locking with Directions ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> and Def. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem18" title="Definition B.18 (Oracle-good Query). ‣ B.5 Why AReW breaks Information Self-locking ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a>, denote the step weight as
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(\omega):=|u_{t}|\,\big|A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\big|\,\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(\omega):=|u_{t}|\,\big|A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\big|\,\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
and let
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(\omega):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(\omega):=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\right].</annotation></semantics></math>
Then
the critique quality is measured by the weighted accuracy</span></p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)\;:=\;\frac{\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}\right]}{\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\right]}\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)\;:=\;\frac{\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}\right]}{\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\right]}\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, the first-order improvement in AS informativeness induced by <span id="A2.Thmtheorem19.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AReW</span> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)\;=\;\eta\,W(\omega)\,\Big(2\,\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)-1\Big)\;+\;o(\eta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)\;=\;\eta\,W(\omega)\,\Big(2\,\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)-1\Big)\;+\;o(\eta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, <span id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AReW</span> improves AS informativeness beyond the baseline
update if and only if
<math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)&gt;\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)&gt;\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Proofs</h3>

<section id="A2.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.6.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Proposition B.10 (AS-channel outcome advantages). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a turn <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{0,\ldots,H-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and condition on the current on-policy model belief
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any query <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the one-step next belief
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)}</annotation></semantics></math> as the belief obtained by executing <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}=q</annotation></semantics></math>, observing
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{t}=\mathsf{O}(s^{\star},q)</annotation></semantics></math> (deterministic), and sampling the BT update
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t+1}=(b,q,o_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t+1}=(b,q,o_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the corresponding one-step potential change
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)}:=\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})-\Psi(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)}:=\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})-\Psi(b)</annotation></semantics></math>, and its one-sided parts
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q):=(\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q):=(\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q):=(-\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)})_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q):=(-\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)})_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the scalar identity <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x)_{+}-(-x)_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x)_{+}-(-x)_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> applied to <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have the decomposition</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)}\;=\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\;-\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\Psi_{t}^{(q)}\;=\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\;-\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">equivalently,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\;=\;\Psi(b)\;+\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\;-\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\;=\;\Psi(b)\;+\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\;-\;I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking conditional expectations given <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}=q</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]=\Psi(b)+\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]=\Psi(b)+\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Assumption B.4. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> states that, for any <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},-}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is independent of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, subtracting equation <a href="#A2.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> for two queries <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b,q\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q^{\prime})})\mid b,q^{\prime}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\mid b,q\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q^{\prime})\mid b,q^{\prime}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b,q\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q^{\prime})})\mid b,q^{\prime}\right]=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\mid b,q\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q^{\prime})\mid b,q^{\prime}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption B.5. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, along on-policy rollouts,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}\right]\leq C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}\right]\leq C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for any realized <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> in the support of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]\leq C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[I_{t}^{\mathrm{M},+}(q)\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]\leq C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. <a href="#A2.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and <a href="#A2.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> yields the bound on the
range of the conditional mean next-step confidence:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{q}\ \mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]-\inf_{q}\ \mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]\ \leq\ C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{q}\ \mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]-\inf_{q}\ \mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]\ \leq\ C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q\in\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now define the conditional mean terminal confidence given the current belief at time <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t+1,H}(b^{\prime}):=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}}=b^{\prime}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t+1,H}(b^{\prime}):=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M}}=b^{\prime}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem6" title="Assumption B.6. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> implies that <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t+1,H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t+1,H}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>:
for any realizable <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\prime},\tilde{b}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\prime},\tilde{b}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|G_{t+1,H}(b^{\prime})-G_{t+1,H}(\tilde{b}^{\prime})\big|\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,\big|\Psi(b^{\prime})-\Psi(\tilde{b}^{\prime})\big|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|G_{t+1,H}(b^{\prime})-G_{t+1,H}(\tilde{b}^{\prime})\big|\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,\big|\Psi(b^{\prime})-\Psi(\tilde{b}^{\prime})\big|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Now define the query-conditioned mean terminal confidence at time <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{H}(q):=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{H}(q):=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By the tower property,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{H}(q)=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[G_{t+1,H}(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{H}(q)=\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[G_{t+1,H}(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\ \middle|\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">At this point, we use the fact that <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t+1,H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t+1,H}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz in <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> and combine it with
the cancellation structure already captured in equation <a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>:
the induced range of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{H}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{H}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by applying
equation <a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> to the extremal conditional means, giving</span></p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sup_{q}m_{H}(q)-\inf_{q}m_{H}(q)\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,\Big(\sup_{q}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q]-\inf_{q}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q]\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{q}m_{H}(q)-\inf_{q}m_{H}(q)\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,\Big(\sup_{q}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q]-\inf_{q}\mathbb{E}_{\omega}[\Psi(b_{t+1}^{\mathrm{M},(q)})\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b,\ q_{t}=q]\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Combining equation <a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> with equation <a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{q}m_{H}(q)-\inf_{q}m_{H}(q)\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{q}m_{H}(q)-\inf_{q}m_{H}(q)\ \leq\ \kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)=f(m_{H}(q))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)=f(m_{H}(q)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-\inf_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\leq L_{R}\,\big(\sup_{q}m_{H}(q)-\inf_{q}m_{H}(q)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-\inf_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\leq L_{R}\,\big(\sup_{q}m_{H}(q)-\inf_{q}m_{H}(q)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging equation <a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-\inf_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\ \leq\ L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-\inf_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\ \leq\ L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V^{J,Q}_{t}(b)=\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b)}[Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{J,Q}_{t}(b)=\mathbb{E}_{q\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b)}[Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)]</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)\}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence for any executed <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q_{t})|=\big|Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q_{t})-V^{J,Q}_{t}(b)\big|\leq\sup_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-\inf_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q_{t})|=\big|Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q_{t})-V^{J,Q}_{t}(b)\big|\leq\sup_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q)-\inf_{q}Q^{J,Q}_{t}(b,q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with equation <a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})|\leq L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})|\leq L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{J,Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\,A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{J,Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\,A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking norms and applying Jensen and the triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big\|\cdot\big|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\big|\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big\|\cdot\big|A^{J,Q}_{t}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}},q_{t})\big|\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Assumption B.9. ‣ B.3 Projected Drifts and the 2D Locking Regime ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a> gives
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot)\|\leq G_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot)\|\leq G_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> a.s., hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq G_{Q}\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\big[\big|A^{J,Q}_{t}\big|\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq G_{Q}\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\big[\big|A^{J,Q}_{t}\big|\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem10" title="Proposition B.10 (AS-channel outcome advantages). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.10</span></a> to each <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq G_{Q}\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\leq H\,G_{Q}\,L_{R}\kappa_{c}C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq G_{Q}\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}L_{R}\,\kappa_{c}\,C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\leq H\,G_{Q}\,L_{R}\kappa_{c}C_{\max}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.6.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem11" title="Proposition B.11 (BT-channel outcome advantages). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a turn <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Condition on the BT context <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and draw two independent samples
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B,B^{\prime}\overset{\mathrm{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em">.</mo></mrow></mover><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B,B^{\prime}\overset{\mathrm{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\pi_{\omega}^{U}(\cdot\mid c_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y:=Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B),\qquad Y^{\prime}:=Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B^{\prime}),\qquad\bar{Y}:=\mathbb{E}[Y\mid c_{t}]=V_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y:=Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B),\qquad Y^{\prime}:=Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B^{\prime}),\qquad\bar{Y}:=\mathbb{E}[Y\mid c_{t}]=V_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B)=Y-\bar{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B)=Y-\bar{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for any fixed realization <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=y</annotation></semantics></math>,
Jensen implies <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|y-Y^{\prime}|\mid y,c_{t}]\geq|y-\mathbb{E}[Y^{\prime}\mid c_{t}]|=|y-\bar{Y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|y-Y^{\prime}|\mid y,c_{t}]\geq|y-\mathbb{E}[Y^{\prime}\mid c_{t}]|=|y-\bar{Y}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking expectation over <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[|Y-\bar{Y}|\mid c_{t}\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\big[|Y-Y^{\prime}|\mid c_{t}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[|Y-\bar{Y}|\mid c_{t}\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\big[|Y-Y^{\prime}|\mid c_{t}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\big|A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big|\right]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\big|Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B)-Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B^{\prime})\big|\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\big|A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big|\right]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\big|Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B)-Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},B^{\prime})\big|\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption B.1. ‣ B.1 Notations &amp; Problem Setup ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>,
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[R(\tau)\mid b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}]=f(\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[R(\tau)\mid b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}]=f(\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}))</annotation></semantics></math> for a non-decreasing <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, for any <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{t},b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{t},b)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}))\ \middle|\ c_{t},\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[f(\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}}))\ \middle|\ c_{t},\ b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,b^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,b^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, using <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\,\mathbb{E}[X]-\mathbb{E}[Y]\,|\leq\mathbb{E}[|X-Y|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\,\mathbb{E}[X]-\mathbb{E}[Y]\,|\leq\mathbb{E}[|X-Y|]</annotation></semantics></math>,
Lipschitzness of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, and the elementary inequality <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x-y|\leq x+y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x-y|\leq x+y</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big|Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b)-Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b^{\prime})\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big|Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b)-Q_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b^{\prime})\big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{R}\Big(\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b]+\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b^{\prime}]\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{R}\Big(\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b]+\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b^{\prime}]\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Along any continuation after time <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})=\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}})\big)\ \leq\ \Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}}))_{+}=\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})=\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}})\big)\ \leq\ \Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}}))_{+}=\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking conditional expectation given <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b)</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b]\ \leq\ \Psi(b)\ +\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{M}})\mid c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b]\ \leq\ \Psi(b)\ +\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By iterated expectations,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbb{E}[I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\mid h_{k+1}]\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathbb{E}[I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\mid h_{k+1}]\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\kappa_{U}\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{B}})\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\kappa_{U}\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{B}})\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">At this point, the right-hand side is the <em id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">remaining Bayesian truth-gain</em> along the realized transcript.
Since our main statement is in terms of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> (Def. <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition B.2. ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>),
we use the following mild presentation-level observation:
conditioning the same parametric query policy <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\omega}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\omega}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> on a <em id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">more accurate</em> belief (oracle belief <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>)
cannot decrease its expected Bayesian truth-gain, so the expected remaining transcript gain is upper bounded by the
oracle-belief MDP gain.
Concretely, we bound</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{B}})\big)\right]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{\mathrm{B}}}\big[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}})\big]=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\omega}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{B}})\big)\right]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{\mathrm{B}}}\big[\Psi(b_{H}^{\mathrm{B}})-\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{B}})\big]=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">and hence (by dropping conditioning and applying tower property) from equation <a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]\ \leq\ \kappa_{U}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{k=t}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}\ \middle|\ c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}=b\right]\ \leq\ \kappa_{U}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining equation <a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, equation <a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>,
equation <a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, and equation <a href="#A2.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.2 Proof of Proposition ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, and averaging over <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B,B^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B,B^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big|A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big|\right]\ \leq\ 2L_{R}\Big(\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})]+\kappa_{U}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\big|A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\big|\right]\ \leq\ 2L_{R}\Big(\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})]+\kappa_{U}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to control <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})]</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})]+C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})]+C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Along any rollout,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})=\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}})\big)\ \leq\ \Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}})\big)_{+}\ \leq\ \Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=0}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})=\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}})\big)\ \leq\ \Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}\big(\Psi(b_{k+1}^{\mathrm{M}})-\Psi(b_{k}^{\mathrm{M}})\big)_{+}\ \leq\ \Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})+\sum_{k=0}^{H-1}I_{k}^{\mathrm{M},+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation yields <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})]\leq\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})]+C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})]\leq\mathbb{E}[\Psi(b_{0}^{\mathrm{M}})]+C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>,
which proves the first inequality in the proposition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{J,U}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\,A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{J,U}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau\sim\pi_{\omega}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H}\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\,A_{t}^{J,U}(c_{t},b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking norms, applying Jensen, and using Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem9" title="Assumption B.9. ‣ B.3 Projected Drifts and the 2D Locking Regime ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.9</span></a> (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}\|\leq G_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}\|\leq G_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> a.s.) gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\leq\sum_{t=0}^{H}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\|\cdot|A_{t}^{J,U}|\big]\leq(H+1)G_{U}\cdot\max_{0\leq t\leq H}\mathbb{E}[|A_{t}^{J,U}|]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\leq\sum_{t=0}^{H}\mathbb{E}\big[\|\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{U}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{M}}\mid c_{t})\|\cdot|A_{t}^{J,U}|\big]\leq(H+1)G_{U}\cdot\max_{0\leq t\leq H}\mathbb{E}[|A_{t}^{J,U}|].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the established bound on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|A_{t}^{J,U}|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|A_{t}^{J,U}|]</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.6.3 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem12" title="Proposition B.12 (AS projected drift is controlled by BT level). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.12</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)=\omega+\eta g_{J,Q}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)=\omega+\eta g_{J,Q}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption B.8 (Local first-order expandability of indices). ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a> (first-order expandability of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega))-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta)=\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega))-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta)=\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the positive part and using <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x+y)_{+}\leq x_{+}+|y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x+y)_{+}\leq x_{+}+|y|</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\Big(\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta)\Big)_{+}\leq\eta\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}+|o(\eta)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\Big(\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta)\Big)_{+}\leq\eta\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}+|o(\eta)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Next, apply Cauchy–Schwarz and the gradient bound <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}\leq\big|\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle\big|\leq\|\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\|\cdot\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq G_{I}\,\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}\leq\big|\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{J,Q}(\omega)\big\rangle\big|\leq\|\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\|\cdot\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq G_{I}\,\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using the assumed norm control <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq K_{Q}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,Q}(\omega)\|\leq K_{Q}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\leq\eta\,G_{I}\,K_{Q}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)+|o(\eta)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{Q}^{+}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\leq\eta\,G_{I}\,K_{Q}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)+|o(\eta)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, absorb <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|o(\eta)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|o(\eta)|</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|o(\eta)|/\eta\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|o(\eta)|/\eta\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>)
to obtain the claimed bound with <math id="A2.SS6.SSS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:=G_{I}K_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:=G_{I}K_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.6.4 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition B.13 (BT projected drift is controlled by AS and BT levels). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega)=\omega+\eta g_{J,U}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega)=\omega+\eta g_{J,U}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption B.8 (Local first-order expandability of indices). ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a> (first-order expandability of <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega))-C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)=\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ \mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta)=\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega))-C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)=\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ \mathcal{T}_{U}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta)=\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking positive parts and using <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x+y)_{+}\leq x_{+}+|y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x+y)_{+}\leq x_{+}+|y|</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)=\Big(\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta)\Big)_{+}\leq\eta\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}+|o(\eta)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)=\Big(\eta\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle+o(\eta)\Big)_{+}\leq\eta\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}+|o(\eta)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Cauchy–Schwarz and the gradient bound <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\|\leq G_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}\leq\big|\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle\big|\leq\|\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\|\cdot\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\leq G_{C}\,\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big(\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle\Big)_{+}\leq\big|\big\langle\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),\ g_{J,U}(\omega)\big\rangle\big|\leq\|\nabla_{\omega}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\|\cdot\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\leq G_{C}\,\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using the assumed norm control on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\ \leq\ K_{U,I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ +\ K_{U,C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{J,U}(\omega)\|\ \leq\ K_{U,I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\ +\ K_{U,C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\leq\eta\,G_{C}\Big(K_{U,I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+K_{U,C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\Big)+|o(\eta)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>U</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{U}^{+}C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\leq\eta\,G_{C}\Big(K_{U,I}\,\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+K_{U,C}\,C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\Big)+|o(\eta)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Absorbing <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|o(\eta)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|o(\eta)|</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> yields the stated bound with
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{I}:=G_{C}K_{U,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{I}:=G_{C}K_{U,I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{C}:=G_{C}K_{U,C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{C}:=G_{C}K_{U,C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.6.5 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem17" title="Proposition B.17. ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.17</span></a></h4>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> term in Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem14" title="Theorem B.14 (2D one-sided self-locking). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a> is uniform over
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,\eta_{0}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,\eta_{0}]</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, the remainder satisfies the componentwise bound
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|o(\eta)\|_{\infty}\leq c_{0}\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|o(\eta)\|_{\infty}\leq c_{0}\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Set <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C:=c_{0}/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C:=c_{0}/m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the capability vector (boldface)</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(\omega):=\begin{pmatrix}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\\
C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2},\quad M:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\alpha\\
\beta_{I}&amp;\beta_{C}\end{pmatrix},\quad\mathbf{1}:=(1,1)^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>α</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(\omega):=\begin{pmatrix}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)\\
C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega)\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2},\quad M:=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\alpha\\
\beta_{I}&amp;\beta_{C}\end{pmatrix},\quad\mathbf{1}:=(1,1)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Inside <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem14" title="Theorem B.14 (2D one-sided self-locking). ‣ B.4 2D One-Sided Self-Locking via Projected Drifts ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a> yields the componentwise bound</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{+}\mathbf{x}(\omega)\ \preceq\ \eta\,M\,\mathbf{x}(\omega)\ +\ c_{0}\eta^{2}\,\mathbf{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{+}\mathbf{x}(\omega)\ \preceq\ \eta\,M\,\mathbf{x}(\omega)\ +\ c_{0}\eta^{2}\,\mathbf{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, for any scalar <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leq z_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leq z_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence any increment in <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded above by its positive part.
Therefore, an upper envelope for the accumulation of positive gains is given by the deterministic recursion</span></p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{k+1}\ \preceq\ (\mathrm{I}+\eta M)\,\mathbf{x}_{k}\ +\ c_{0}\eta^{2}\,\mathbf{1},\qquad\mathbf{x}_{0}:=\mathbf{x}(\omega_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{k+1}\ \preceq\ (\mathrm{I}+\eta M)\,\mathbf{x}_{k}\ +\ c_{0}\eta^{2}\,\mathbf{1},\qquad\mathbf{x}_{0}:=\mathbf{x}(\omega_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}:=\|\mathbf{x}_{k}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}:=\|\mathbf{x}_{k}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> on equation <a href="#A2.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.6.5 Proof of Corollary ‣ B.6 Proofs ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> and using
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{I}+\eta M\|_{\infty}=1+\eta m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{I}+\eta M\|_{\infty}=1+\eta m</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k+1}\ \leq\ (1+\eta m)\,y_{k}\ +\ c_{0}\eta^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k+1}\ \leq\ (1+\eta m)\,y_{k}\ +\ c_{0}\eta^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Unrolling this scalar recursion and using <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta m)^{k}\leq e^{k\eta m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta m)^{k}\leq e^{k\eta m}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}\ \leq\ e^{k\eta m}\Big(y_{0}+\tfrac{c_{0}}{m}\eta\Big)\ -\ \tfrac{c_{0}}{m}\eta\ =\ e^{k\eta m}\Big(y_{0}+C\eta\Big)\ -\ C\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}\ \leq\ e^{k\eta m}\Big(y_{0}+\tfrac{c_{0}}{m}\eta\Big)\ -\ \tfrac{c_{0}}{m}\eta\ =\ e^{k\eta m}\Big(y_{0}+C\eta\Big)\ -\ C\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the initialization condition <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega_{0})\leq\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{BT}}(\omega_{0})\leq\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{0}=\|\mathbf{x}_{0}\|_{\infty}\leq\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{0}=\|\mathbf{x}_{0}\|_{\infty}\leq\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, if</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{k\eta m}\Big(\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta\Big)-C\eta\ \leq\ u_{\star}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{k\eta m}\Big(\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta\Big)-C\eta\ \leq\ u_{\star},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">then <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{k}\leq u_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}\leq u_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{k}\preceq(u_{\star},u_{\star})^{\top}\preceq(\delta,\varepsilon)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{k}\preceq(u_{\star},u_{\star})^{\top}\preceq(\delta,\varepsilon)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Solving the inequality for <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\ \leq\ \frac{1}{\eta m}\log\!\Bigg(\frac{u_{\star}+C\eta}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta}\Bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\ \leq\ \frac{1}{\eta m}\log\!\Bigg(\frac{u_{\star}+C\eta}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta}\Bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Choosing</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\Bigg\lfloor\frac{1}{\eta m}\,\log\!\Bigg(\frac{u_{\star}+C\eta}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta}\Bigg)\Bigg\rfloor_{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\Bigg\lfloor\frac{1}{\eta m}\,\log\!\Bigg(\frac{u_{\star}+C\eta}{\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega_{0})+C\eta}\Bigg)\Bigg\rfloor_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">ensures the above condition holds for all integers <math id="A2.SS6.SSS5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{0,1,\ldots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{0,1,\ldots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>, proving the claimed finite-horizon trapping
(escape-time lower bound) under the projected drift envelope.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.7 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem19" title="Proposition B.19 (Weighted accuracy characterizes AReW improvement). ‣ Efficacy of AReW and weighted accuracy. ‣ B.5 Why AReW breaks Information Self-locking ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.19</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega=\eta\,g_{J,Q}(\omega)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega=\eta\,g_{J,Q}(\omega),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega=\eta\,g_{J,Q}(\omega)+\eta\,\lambda_{Q}g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>aux</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega=\eta\,g_{J,Q}(\omega)+\eta\,\lambda_{Q}g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption B.8 (Local first-order expandability of indices). ‣ B.2 Two Capability Indices ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>, for <math id="A2.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\prime}=\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\prime}=\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and for <math id="A2.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega^{\prime}=\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega^{\prime}=\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\in\mathcal{R}_{\delta,\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)+\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\omega\Big\rangle+o(\eta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting equation <a href="#A2.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.7 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a> from equation <a href="#A2.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.7 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\Big\rangle+o(\eta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ \widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\Big\rangle+o(\eta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the update definitions,
<math id="A2.SS7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)=\eta\,\lambda_{Q}\,g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>aux</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)-\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)=\eta\,\lambda_{Q}\,g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>,
so</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\widehat{\mathcal{T}}_{Q}(\omega)\big)-\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}\!\big(\mathcal{T}_{Q}(\omega)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta\,\lambda_{Q}\,\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega)\Big\rangle+o(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>aux</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta\,\lambda_{Q}\,\Big\langle\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega),\ g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega)\Big\rangle+o(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=:\eta\,\lambda_{Q}\,\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)\ +o(\eta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=:\eta\,\lambda_{Q}\,\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)\ +o(\eta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We expand <math id="A2.SS7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the oracle-belief MDP,
<math id="A2.SS7.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}}[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}I_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}}[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}I_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}]</annotation></semantics></math>
is a finite-horizon policy objective with action <math id="A2.SS7.p4.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}\sim\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(\cdot\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus, the policy-gradient theorem yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\,s_{t}(\omega)\right],\qquad s_{t}(\omega)=\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>th</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\omega}\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{th}}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\,s_{t}(\omega)\right],\qquad s_{t}(\omega)=\nabla_{\omega}\log\pi_{\omega}^{Q}(q_{t}\mid b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The likelihood-gap auxiliary objective in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Injecting directional critiques into policy-gradient ‣ 4 Breaking Self-Locking with Directions ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> induces an additive update component of the form</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}u_{t}(z)\,s_{t}(\omega)\right],\qquad u_{t}(z)=|u_{t}|\,z_{t},\ \ |u_{t}|\geq 0,\ \ z_{t}\in\{+1,-1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>aux</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathrm{aux},Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\mathrm{B}}}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}u_{t}(z)\,s_{t}(\omega)\right],\qquad u_{t}(z)=|u_{t}|\,z_{t},\ \ |u_{t}|\geq 0,\ \ z_{t}\in\{+1,-1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By bilinearity and exchanging expectation with finite sums,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)\ \propto\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\Big\langle\sum_{t}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}\,s_{t},\ \sum_{u}b_{u}\,s_{u}\Big\rangle\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t,u}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}\,b_{u}\,\langle s_{t},s_{u}\rangle\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)\ \propto\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\Big\langle\sum_{t}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}\,s_{t},\ \sum_{u}b_{u}\,s_{u}\Big\rangle\right]=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t,u}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}\,b_{u}\,\langle s_{t},s_{u}\rangle\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">For simplicity of analysis, we remove the cross-time terms, giving</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\,u_{t}(z)\,\|s_{t}(\omega)\|^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}(b_{t}^{\mathrm{B}},q_{t})\,u_{t}(z)\,\|s_{t}(\omega)\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}=|A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}|\,y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}=|A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}|\,y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}=\mathrm{sign}(A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})\in\{\pm 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}=\mathrm{sign}(A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}})\in\{\pm 1\}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}=|u_{t}|\,z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}=|u_{t}|\,z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}\in\{\pm 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}\in\{\pm 1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then each summand becomes</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}\,b_{t}\,\|s_{t}\|^{2}=|u_{t}|\,|A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}|\,\|s_{t}\|^{2}\,(z_{t}y_{t})=w_{t}(\omega)\,(z_{t}y_{t})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}\,b_{t}\,\|s_{t}\|^{2}=|u_{t}|\,|A_{t}^{\mathrm{B}}|\,\|s_{t}\|^{2}\,(z_{t}y_{t})=w_{t}(\omega)\,(z_{t}y_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the weight defined above.
Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\,z_{t}y_{t}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t=0}^{H-1}w_{t}(\omega)\,z_{t}y_{t}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}y_{t}=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}y_{t}=+1</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}=y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}=y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}y_{t}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}y_{t}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}\neq y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}\neq y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.SS7.p6.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{t}y_{t}=2\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}y_{t}=2\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma_{Q}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t}w_{t}(\omega)\,\big(2\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}-1\big)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t}w_{t}(\omega)\,\big(2\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}-1\big)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t}w_{t}(\omega)\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}\right]-\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t}w_{t}(\omega)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t}w_{t}(\omega)\,\mathbf{1}\{z_{t}=y_{t}\}\right]-\mathbb{E}\!\left[\sum_{t}w_{t}(\omega)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W(\omega)\,\Big(2\,\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)-1\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W(\omega)\,\Big(2\,\mathrm{Acc}_{Q}(\omega)-1\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is equation <a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proposition B.19 (Weighted accuracy characterizes AReW improvement). ‣ Efficacy of AReW and weighted accuracy. ‣ B.5 Why AReW breaks Information Self-locking ‣ Appendix B More Details on the Theory ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. The final equivalence follows immediately when <math id="A2.SS7.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W(\omega)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W(\omega)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Setup Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Dataset Details and Prompt Templates</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present more details for the datasets and tasks evaluated in this work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Preference Estimation – Gated (PE-G)</span>, adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Badola et al. (2025)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zou et al. (2026)</a></cite>.
Adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Badola et al. (2025)</a></cite>,
Gated-PE is an interactive preference inference task under constrained information acquisition.
The agent is given a finite set of items <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\{x_{1},\dots,x_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\{x_{1},\dots,x_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each item <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by a known attribute vector <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The user is characterized by an unknown latent preference vector <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}^{\star}\in[0,1]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}^{\star}\in[0,1]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Through interaction, the agent maintains and iteratively refines an estimate <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{t}\in[0,1]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{t}\in[0,1]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> of this latent preference.
At each decision point, the agent actively selects a low-dimensional attribute subspace <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}\subseteq\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}\subseteq\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> and an item comparison <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},x_{j})\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},x_{j})\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> designed to elicit the user’s preference feedback restricted to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Based on the observed feedback, the agent updates its belief state.
The objective is to accurately recover <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> under sparse, outcome-based supervision.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MediQ</span>, adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
Adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2024)</a></cite>,
MediQ is an interactive medical inference task that models hypothesis-level belief tracking under partial observability.
The agent is provided with a clinical vignette and an associated medical question whose answer lies in a finite hypothesis set of size <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>.
The agent maintains a belief state <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{t}\in[0,1]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{t}\in[0,1]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each dimension represents the current support for a candidate hypothesis.
Through iterative interaction, the agent actively queries the LLM-simulated user for diagnostic information, receives structured feedback, and updates each hypothesis score accordingly.
The learning objective is to progressively concentrate belief mass onto the correct hypothesis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FloDial</span>, adapted from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Raghu et al. (2021)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. (2024)</a></cite> consists of multi-turn diagnostic dialogues for resolving user-reported issues.
It provides a scenario where a
customer support technician interacts with customers to identify and resolve faults or issues within
computer systems, electronic devices, machinery, or other complex systems. The agent simulates the customer support
technician, which chat with the customer to further check the specific issues of device through multi-turn interactions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Baseline Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we introduce RL algorithms used in our experiments.
Formally, given an actor model <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the likelihood of a response <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> to a query <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> under the policy <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is modeled as <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=\prod_{t=1}^{|y|}\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}|x,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y|x)=\prod_{t=1}^{|y|}\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}|x,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a query-response pair <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, a verifier <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> generates its reward <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite>
employs the following objective for policy optimization:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{PPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},\,y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{1}{|y|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y|}\min\left(w_{t}(\theta)\widehat{A}_{t},\,\mathrm{clip}\left(w_{t}(\theta),1-{\varepsilon},1+{\varepsilon}\right)\widehat{A}_{t}\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>PPO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>clip</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{PPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},\,y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|x)}\left[\frac{1}{|y|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y|}\min\left(w_{t}(\theta)\widehat{A}_{t},\,\mathrm{clip}\left(w_{t}(\theta),1-{\varepsilon},1+{\varepsilon}\right)\widehat{A}_{t}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the importance ratio of the token <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as
<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}|x,y_{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{t}|x,y_{&lt;t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}|x,y_{&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{t}|x,y_{&lt;t})}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the advantage <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is typically computed via Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2015</a>)</cite> with temporal-difference errors, and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the clipping range of importance ratios.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> proposes computing the relative advantage of each response within a group of responses of the same query using the following objective (omitting the KL regularization term):</p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x,\,\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\min\left(w_{i,t}(\theta)\widehat{A}_{i,t},\,\mathrm{clip}\left(w_{i,t}(\theta),1-{\varepsilon},1+{\varepsilon}\right)\widehat{A}_{i,t}\right)\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x,\,\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}}\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\min\left(w_{i,t}(\theta)\widehat{A}_{i,t},\,\mathrm{clip}\left(w_{i,t}(\theta),1-{\varepsilon},1+{\varepsilon}\right)\widehat{A}_{i,t}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is the group size. The importance ratio <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i,t}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i,t}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and advantage <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{A}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{A}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> of token <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{i,t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})},\,\,\widehat{A}_{i,t}=\frac{r(x,y_{i})-\mathrm{mean}\left(\{r(x,y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}\right)}{\mathrm{std}\left(\{r(x,y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}\right)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.507em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>mean</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{i,t}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})},\,\,\widehat{A}_{i,t}=\frac{r(x,y_{i})-\mathrm{mean}\left(\{r(x,y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}\right)}{\mathrm{std}\left(\{r(x,y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">respectively, where all the tokens in <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> share the same advantage.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Group Sequence Policy Optimization (GSPO)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite> extends GRPO by defining the importance ratio at the sequence level with length normalization, with sequence-level clipping, rewarding, and optimization. The objective is:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GSPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x,\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}}\Bigg[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\min\big(s_{i}(\theta)\widehat{A}_{i},\ \operatorname{clip}(s_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\widehat{A}_{i}\big)\Bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GSPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{GSPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x,\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}}\Bigg[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\min\big(s_{i}(\theta)\widehat{A}_{i},\ \operatorname{clip}(s_{i}(\theta),1-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)\widehat{A}_{i}\big)\Bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}(\theta)=\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}|x)}\right)^{1/|y_{i}|}=\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}(\theta)=\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}|x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i}|x)}\right)^{1/|y_{i}|}=\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{|y_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|y_{i}|}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(y_{i,t}|x,y_{i,&lt;t})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Supplementary Implementation Details</h3>

<section id="A3.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.3.1 </span>Additional Setting on Datasets</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide additional implementation details.
The maximum number of interaction turns is set at 10 for PE-G, 12 for PE-F, 8 for MediQ, 10 for FloDial-Easy and FloDial-Hard.
For RL training, we define task-specific rewards aligned with their evaluation metrics:
for PE-G and PE-F, the reward is the similarity improvement compared to the initial default guess (all 0.5), where PE-G leverages binary reward (<math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}[\mathrm{improvement}]&gt;0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>improvement</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}[\mathrm{improvement}]&gt;0.03</annotation></semantics></math>) and PE-F leverages the continuous improvement value (normalized to <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>).
For MediQ and FloDial, the reward is binary, checking if the final decision made by the agents aligns with the ground-truth.
All rewards are provided only at the terminal step of each trajectory, consistent with the outcome-based RL setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The AS and BT proxies on PE and MediQ datasets can be seen in Sec. <a href="#S2" title="2 Self-Locking in Active Reasoning ‣ On Information Self-Locking in Reinforcement Learning for Active Reasoning of LLM agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. For the FloDial dataset, the query is considered as uninformative if the user replies “unknown”, and the BT proxy is defined by whether the agent can increase the confidence of the ground truth when receiving informative feedback.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Critique construction (AS vs. BT).</span>
Across datasets, we use two lightweight stepwise critiques:
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> (AS-channel) evaluates whether the <em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">query step</em> at turn <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> yields informative feedback,
and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}</annotation></semantics></math> (BT-channel) evaluates whether the subsequent <em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">belief update</em> is consistent with that feedback.
Below we summarize the dataset-specific instantiations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PE-G and PE-F.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">AS critique.</em>
Let the action be a comparison between two items, inducing a signed attribute-difference vector
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{ij}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{ij}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> (restricted to the focused coordinates when applicable).
We mark the query as informative if it exhibits a non-trivial trade-off across coordinates, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{t}^{Q}=+1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\exists k,\ell\in[D]\ \text{s.t.}\ m_{ij,k}\,m_{ij,\ell}&lt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{Q}=+1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\exists k,\ell\in[D]\ \text{s.t.}\ m_{ij,k}\,m_{ij,\ell}&lt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and set <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{Q}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{Q}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> for repeated or invalid queries or when <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is one-signed.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">BT critique.</em>
Conditioned on an informative query (<math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{Q}=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{Q}=+1</annotation></semantics></math>), we compare the updated preference estimate <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
against the previous valid estimate <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> using similarity to the ground-truth preference <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=\mathrm{sign}\!\Big(\mathrm{sim}(v_{t},w^{\star})-\mathrm{sim}(v_{t-1},w^{\star})\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.756em;" width="1.756em"><mi>sign</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=\mathrm{sign}\!\Big(\mathrm{sim}(v_{t},w^{\star})-\mathrm{sim}(v_{t-1},w^{\star})\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">and set <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=0</annotation></semantics></math> when the query is uninformative or invalid.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MediQ.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">AS critique.</em>
Let <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the patient feedback to the query at turn <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
We set <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{Q}=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{Q}=+1</annotation></semantics></math> iff the feedback is informative (i.e., not an “Unknown / cannot answer” response)
and the query is not repeated; otherwise <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{Q}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{Q}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
We additionally explore counterfactual pattern (exploration on other datasets as future work).
When counterfactual queries are enabled,
we intervene the belief from the last turn and obtain the counterfactual query.
We then discourage semantic repetition by requiring
the counterfactual query to be sufficiently different from the actual query (measured by token-level overlap),
and mark the step as uninformative when this difference is small.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">BT critique.</em>
Let <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\in[0,1]^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\in[0,1]^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> be the belief over <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> hypotheses and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> the ground-truth hypothesis.
Define the margin</p>
<table id="A3.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{mar}(w_{t};s^{\star}):=w_{t}(s^{\star})-\max_{s\neq s^{\star}}w_{t}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>mar</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{mar}(w_{t};s^{\star}):=w_{t}(s^{\star})-\max_{s\neq s^{\star}}w_{t}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">If the feedback is uninformative, we enforce <em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">invariance</em>:
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=+1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{mar}(w_{t};s^{\star})=\mathrm{mar}(w_{t-1};s^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>mar</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>mar</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{mar}(w_{t};s^{\star})=\mathrm{mar}(w_{t-1};s^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
If the feedback is informative, we employ a counterfactual-consistency check:
We intervene the observation to “unknown” and obtain
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}^{\mathrm{cf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cf</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}^{\mathrm{cf}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a counterfactual update from the same previous belief <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> but from the “unknown” response; then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=+1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\|w_{t}^{\mathrm{cf}}-w_{t-1}\|_{2}\leq\|w_{t}-w_{t-1}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>U</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>cf</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=+1\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\|w_{t}^{\mathrm{cf}}-w_{t-1}\|_{2}\leq\|w_{t}-w_{t-1}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=-1</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FloDial.</span>
<em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">AS critique.</em>
User feedback takes the form <span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Yes/No</span> when the query matches a reference diagnostic item,
and <span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Unknown</span> otherwise. We set</p>
<table id="A3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{Q}=\begin{cases}+1,&amp;\text{if feedback is {Yes}},\\
0,&amp;\text{if feedback is {No}},\\
-1,&amp;\text{if feedback is {Unknown} (no match)}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if feedback is </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Yes</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if feedback is </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">No</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if feedback is </mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Unknown</mtext><mtext> (no match)</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{Q}=\begin{cases}+1,&amp;\text{if feedback is {Yes}},\\
0,&amp;\text{if feedback is {No}},\\
-1,&amp;\text{if feedback is {Unknown} (no match)}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">BT critique.</em>
Let <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\in[0,1]^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\in[0,1]^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be the belief over candidate faults and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> the ground-truth fault.
When the feedback is informative (<span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Yes/No</span>), we encourage increasing confidence on <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=+1\ \Longleftrightarrow\ w_{t}(s^{\star})&gt;w_{t-1}(s^{\star}),\qquad z_{t}^{U}=-1\ \text{otherwise}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=+1\ \Longleftrightarrow\ w_{t}(s^{\star})&gt;w_{t-1}(s^{\star}),\qquad z_{t}^{U}=-1\ \text{otherwise}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.3" class="ltx_p">When the feedback is uninformative (<span id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Unknown</span>), we use an invariance-style rule:
we require the belief to remain unchanged
(e.g., <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{t}^{U}=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{t}^{U}=+1</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A3.SS3.SSS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}=w_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}=w_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.3.2 </span>Training Configurations</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All expriments are trained on a single node with 8 B200 GPUs, based on the implementations of Verl <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. All training tasks on PPO are conducted for 200 steps (GRPO and GSPO 100 steps) with the actor model optimized using a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For distributed training, we adopt Fully Sharded Data
Parallelism (FSDP), using BFloat16 precision throughout both training and evaluation.
For efficient LLM rollouts, we adopt vLLM <span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              <a href="https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/</a></span></span></span> with a tensor parallel size of 1. The rollout sampling uses a temperature of 1.0 for all datasets.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the PPO baseline, we use Generalized
Advantage Estimation (GAE) with parameters <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The clip ratio <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> are set to 0.2. For GRPO training, we sample 3 responses per prompt, and the rollout parameters with the clip ratio are consistent with the PPO setting. For the GSPO algorithm, the clip ratio <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{low}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{low}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{high}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{high}</annotation></semantics></math> are set to 0.0003 and 0.0004, respectively, while others keep consistent with GRPO training.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="970.61" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 970.61" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,970.61) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 964.71 C 0 967.97 2.64 970.61 5.91 970.61 L 471.47 970.61 C 474.73 970.61 477.38 967.97 477.38 964.71 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 946.5 L 475.41 946.5 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 955.1)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Input Prompts for the MovieRec Preference Estimation Dataset</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.35em;--ltx-fo-height:66.55em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="920.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 920.92)" width="544.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.35em;">
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an interactive preference estimation agent. The goal is to infer a user’s
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{len_attributes}</span>-dimensional hidden preference vector on movies through multi-round interaction.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Setup:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- You are given <span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{len_seen}</span> movies, each with scores on
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{len_attributes}</span> dimensions (indexed <math id="A3.F6.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\dots{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_attributes\lx@text@rbrace}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#001473">{len_attributes}</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\dots{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_attributes\lx@text@rbrace}}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{seen_movie_sample}<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Maintain an estimate of the user’s preference vector:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guess: <math id="A3.F6.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_attributes\lx@text@rbrace}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#001473">{len_attributes}</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_attributes\lx@text@rbrace}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Initialization:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guess: <math id="A3.F6.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5,0.5,\dots,0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5,0.5,\dots,0.5</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Interaction Protocol:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Interaction alternates between two types of rounds.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1) <span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action Round (odd-numbered rounds: 1,3,5,…)</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In an Action Round, you must choose which information to query.
You must output exactly:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;interact&gt;
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.13.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Focus: k1,k2,k3</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pair: p1,p2</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/interact&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rules:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Focus must contain exactly three distinct integers in
<math id="A3.F6.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_attributes\lx@text@rbrace}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#001473">{len_attributes}</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_attributes\lx@text@rbrace}}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Ensure that all dimensions receive opportunities to be disambiguated over the course of interaction.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Pair must contain exactly two distinct integers in
<math id="A3.F6.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1,{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_seen\lx@text@rbrace}}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#001473">{len_seen}</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1,{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace len\_seen\lx@text@rbrace}}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Avoid uninformative pairs, such as dominance pairs where one movie is better
on all focused dimensions <math id="A3.F6.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1},k_{2},k_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1},k_{2},k_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">After you output Focus and Pair, the user will provide feedback:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- User Feedback: “Yes”, “No”, or “Equal”.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">“Yes” means <math id="A3.F6.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is preferred when considering only dimensions <math id="A3.F6.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1},k_{2},k_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1},k_{2},k_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.22.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2) <span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.23.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Update Round (even-numbered rounds: 2,4,6,…)</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In an Update Round, you must update the preference estimate based on the most recent
Focus, Pair, and User Feedback.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You must output exactly:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.26" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.26.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;interact&gt;
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.26.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guess: w1,w2,…,w</span><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{len_attributes}
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.26.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/interact&gt;</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.27" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rules:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.28" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Guess must be comma-separated numbers.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.29" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Use the feedback to adjust the relative importance of the focused dimensions
in a way consistent with the observed preference.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.30" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Reasoning:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.31" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Before each <span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.31.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;interact&gt;</span> block, you may briefly reason about what to do in a:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.32" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.32.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;scratch&gt;... &lt;/scratch&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.33" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.2.33.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Round 1 is an Action Round.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A3.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt Template for MovieRec Preference Estimation.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1004.54" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 1004.54" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1004.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 998.64 C 0 1001.9 2.64 1004.54 5.91 1004.54 L 471.47 1004.54 C 474.73 1004.54 477.38 1001.9 477.38 998.64 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 980.43 L 475.41 980.43 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 989.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Input Prompts for the MediQ Dataset</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 15.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.35em;--ltx-fo-height:68.87em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="954.85" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 952.97)" width="544.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.35em;">
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an interactive medical inference agent.
Your goal is to iteratively maintain and refine a 4-dimensional state vector that tracks the relative support for four potential hypotheses associated with a given medical question, through multi-round interaction.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Setup:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- You are given:
(i) a clinical vignette describing a patient scenario, and
(ii) a medical question associated with this scenario.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- The question admits four potential hypotheses, labeled A, B, C, and D.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Maintain a state vector <math id="A3.F7.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{A},w_{B},w_{C},w_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{A},w_{B},w_{C},w_{D})</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="A3.F7.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,
representing your current level of support for each hypothesis.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Initialization:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guess: <math id="A3.F7.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5,0.5,0.5,0.5</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- In each Action round, you can issue <span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">only one</span> query.
The query must be a single, atomic question intended to reduce uncertainty among the four hypotheses;
compound or multi-part questions are not allowed.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Alternating Interaction Protocol:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Interaction alternates between two types of rounds:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1) <span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action Round (odd-numbered rounds: 1,3,5,…)</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- You must output only a query in the exact format:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;interact&gt;
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.13.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Query: …</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/interact&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- After you output a Query, the user will provide feedback.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2) <span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Update Round (even-numbered rounds: 2,4,6,…)</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- You must update and output only the state vector (Guess) based on:
(a) the most recent Query, and
(b) the feedback returned for that Query.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Output in the exact format:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;interact&gt;
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.19.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guess: wA,wB,wC,wD</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/interact&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Guess must be comma-separated numbers.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## State Update Rules (in Update rounds, after feedback):</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Each dimension can be adjusted independently, depending on how the feedback affects that hypothesis.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Query Policy (in Action rounds):</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Ask atomic, clinically meaningful queries that help differentiate among the four hypotheses.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Avoid repeating previously asked queries.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.27" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Before each <span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.27.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;interact&gt;</span> block, briefly reason (in a few sentences) about what you should do in a:
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.27.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;scratch&gt;... &lt;/scratch&gt;</span> block, following the protocol above.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.28" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let’s get started:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.29" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Clinical Vignette: <span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.29.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{clinical_vignette}</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.30" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Medical Question: <span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.30.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{medical_question}</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.31" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Potential Hypotheses: <span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.31.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{potential_hypotheses}</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.32" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.2.32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Round 1 is an Action Round. Output your first Query.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A3.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt Template for MediQ.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F8.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1191.58" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 1191.58" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1191.58) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 1185.67 C 0 1188.93 2.64 1191.58 5.91 1191.58 L 471.47 1191.58 C 474.73 1191.58 477.38 1188.93 477.38 1185.67 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 1167.47 L 475.41 1167.47 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 1176.06)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Input Prompts for the FloDial Dataset</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 15.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.35em;--ltx-fo-height:82.39em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="1141.89" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1140.01)" width="544.49"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.35em;">
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are an interactive troubleshooting diagnosis agent.
Your goal is to iteratively maintain and refine a state vector that tracks the relative plausibility of
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{num_candidates}</span> candidate descriptions for a given problem, through multi-round interaction.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Setup:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- You are given:
(i) a task description describing the user’s problem, and
(ii) a list of <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{num_candidates}</span> candidate descriptions.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Each candidate is a possible explanation, diagnosis, or resolution suggestion related to the problem.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Exactly <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">one</span> of the candidate descriptions best matches the actual situation described by the user.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Your goal is to identify which candidate description is the most consistent with the situation,
by asking diagnostic yes/no questions.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Maintain a state vector <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace num\_candidates\lx@text@rbrace}}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#001473">{num_candidates}</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{1},w_{2},\dots,w_{{\color[rgb]{0,0.08,0.45}{\texttt{\lx@text@lbrace num\_candidates\lx@text@rbrace}}}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
where each <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, representing your current level of support for candidate <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Initialization:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guess: <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5,0.5,\dots,0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5,0.5,\dots,0.5</annotation></semantics></math> (length <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{num_candidates}</span>)</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- In each Action Round, you issue <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">only one</span> query.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">## Alternating Interaction Protocol:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Interaction alternates between two types of rounds:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1) <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Action Round (odd-numbered rounds: 1,3,5,…)</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Output only a query in the exact format:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;interact&gt;
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.15.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Query: …</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/interact&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- The query must be a single, atomic yes/no diagnostic question intended to reduce uncertainty among
the <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{num_candidates}</span> candidate descriptions.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Avoid repeating previously asked queries.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Do <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not</span> directly ask whether a specific candidate description is correct or incorrect.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Compound or multi-part questions are not allowed.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2) <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Update Round (even-numbered rounds: 2,4,6,…)</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Update and output only the state vector (Guess), based on the most recent query and the feedback returned for that query.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Output in the exact format:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.24" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;interact&gt;
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.24.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guess: w1,w2,…,w</span><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{num_candidates}
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.24.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;/interact&gt;</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Each <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> must remain within <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- If the user replies “Unknown”, leave all weights unchanged.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.27" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">- Each dimension can be adjusted independently by <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> (not changed), <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A3.F8.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.1</annotation></semantics></math>,
depending on how the feedback affects that candidate.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.28" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Before each <span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.28.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;interact&gt;</span> block, briefly reason (in a few sentences) in a
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.28.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;scratch&gt;... &lt;/scratch&gt;</span> block about what to ask or how the feedback affects your belief.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.29" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let’s get started.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.30" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task Description:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.31" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.31.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{task_description}<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.31.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.32" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Candidate Descriptions:</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.33" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.33.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#001473;">{candidate_descriptions}<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.33.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.34" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.2.34.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Round 1 is an Action Round. Output your first query.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A3.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt Template for FloDial.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">langley00</span></cite></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
